ors\n   done\n   ```\n3. Invalidate the CDN afterwards — the old headers are cached at the edge too.\n4. Put this loop in the deploy script, not in your shell history.\n\n**Verify:** `curl -sI https://your-site/ | grep -i content-type` must return `text/html`, and the same check on your main JavaScript bundle must return `application/javascript` — not `binary/octet-stream`. A 200 status alone proves nothing here. Then load the site in a browser that has never seen it.\nsrc/index.html:6:<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\">\nsrc/index.html:12:<script src=\"/booking.js\"></script>\nsrc/clases.html:2:<html lang=\"es\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Clases</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\"></head>\nsrc/clases.html:3:<body><h1>Clases</h1><ul><li>Torno inicial, sábados</li><li>Modelado, martes</li></ul><div id=\"booking\"></div><script src=\"/booking.js\"></script></body></html>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01U1ZYqw2UDTwimtzU1ZZXzA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
