{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAsR3GJMoz2YuTZoQu8c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated `scripts/deploy.sh` so every upload now sets a `Cache-Control` header, and wrote up the change in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing was deployed or run against AWS; I only checked that the script parses (`bash -n`).\n\n- **Short (5 minutes, `public, max-age=300`):** the HTML pages, `booking.js` and `styles.css`.\n- **Long (30 days, `public, max-age=2592000`):** everything in `assets/`.\n\n**How the new deploy works:**\n- **Uploads:** it uses `aws s3 cp` instead of `sync`. `sync` skips files that haven't changed, so the files already in the bucket would never get the header. Uploads go in order (assets, then JS/CSS, then HTML) so a new page never points at a file that isn't up yet.\n- **Cleanup:** `sync --delete` still runs afterwards, but only to remove deleted files. The CloudFront invalidation is unchanged.\n- **Content type stays correct:** your note in `notes/` describes the site being served as `binary/octet-stream` after a header change. This script can't cause that, because it uploads from local files and the type is still set from each file's extension, as before. I left a comment in the script warning against switching to that method.\n\n**Choices you may want to change** (both values are at the top of the script):\n- **Why 30 days and not a year:** files in `assets/` keep the same names when they change (`logo.png`, `mark.svg`). If you change the logo without renaming it, visitors could see the old one for up to 30 days. If you ever change an asset, give it a new name.\n- **CSS:** you didn't mention it, so I treated it like the JS, since its name also stays the same between deploys.\n- **People with the old file already cached:** visitors who already have the old `booking.js` may keep it until their browser decides it's stale. The new header takes effect from their next download.\n\nAfter the next real deploy, check the headers with `curl -sI` on `/`, `/booking.js` and `/assets/logo.png`. Each should show the right content type and the matching cache time; the exact commands are in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1181,"cache_read_input_tokens":23856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1181},"output_tokens":684,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"570dba33-c106-44c6-b929-f944bfdd609b","uuid":"d6353e38-b7e6-43ba-aea4-5b14d360748c","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:16:28.331Z","request_id":"req_011CgAsR2yvZ5JFMd8NhNQzc"}
